# Databases that install-databases.sh bakes into each package_tests:<os> image,
# all from Percona's repositories. This is also what the playbooks expect: each
# line becomes <database>-<version> in their enabled_db (ps-8.4), and a test
# fails if that database is missing or at another version.
#
# database    ps (Percona Server for MySQL) or pg (Percona Distribution for
#             PostgreSQL). Each needs an install_<name> function in
#             install-databases.sh.
# version     the series to install, at its newest release: 8.0 or 8.4 for ps,
#             14 to 18 for pg
# repository  the percona-release channel: release, testing or experimental
#
# An OS gets only the databases listed for it, but every OS in
# build-package-test-images.yml needs at least one line.
#
# os          database  version  repository
ol8           ps        8.4      release
ol9           ps        8.4      release
ol10          ps        8.4      testing    # no el10 build in release yet
debian12      ps        8.4      release
debian13      ps        8.4      release
ubuntu2204    ps        8.4      release
ubuntu2404    ps        8.4      release
ubuntu2604    ps        8.4      release

ol8           pg        18       release
ol9           pg        18       release
ol10          pg        18       release
debian12      pg        18       release
debian13      pg        18       release
ubuntu2204    pg        17       release
ubuntu2404    pg        17       release
ubuntu2604    pg        18       release
